# Process 3.4, the body of portal.router.ServeHTTP: the portal handler's
# answer to each request that box 9.4 sends it. The response writer of the
# request passes unchanged from box 9.4 to box 3.4.3, and the access passes
# through box 3.4.4. Each box reads the router's sites, hooks and routes as
# its receiver. Every page's navigation bar ends with the view's account
# links, and a chat page's GET keeps them in its page session, from
# portal.AccountLinksOf. Box 3.4.3 also
# draws the chat's state and I/O behind its routes. A chat page's GET asks
# the embedding program for the reader ID and the page access, and with a
# reader hook the page answers privately (chat.Chat.privatePage). The page
# session leaves in the page's response and comes back at the join, over the
# chat's socket, which lives in the route of its upgrade request; each
# question that arrives there reads and writes the question counts and the
# conversations, and asks the chat model. The counts and the
# conversations belong to the chat that box 6 of flow.dfd keeps across
# snapshots. The exchanges with the embedding program happen only in a
# program that sets the hooks; docportal sets none. A request from the
# previews handler of flow.11.dfd carries the banner in its context, and the
# pages of box 3.4.3 draw it above the navigation bar; a page with the
# notice clears the notice cookie of the previews handler in its response.
# By hand: dfd --box 300x150 --per-row 5 --number --number-prefix 3.4. docs/flow.3.4.dfd -o flow.3.4.svg

{9.4 Answer each request with the portal handler of the snapshot in service}
> request
[3.4.1. Ask the access hook for the access of the request's reader, once: Everything without a hook, and an access that allows nothing after an error or a nil access, whose cause goes to the log
 (portal.router.readerAccess)]
    > request
    < access, error
    <Embedding program>
    > hook problem
    <Log>
> request
[3.4.4. Ask the account hook for the account links of the request's reader, once: none without a hook
 (portal.router.accountLinks)]
    > request
    < account links
    <Embedding program>
> access, account links
[3.4.2. Build the reader's view: the access, the account links and the reader's sites, a copy of the site of each visible portal with only its visible sections
 so that every page of the request reads only what is visible to the reader and ends every navigation bar with the reader's account links
 (portal.router.viewFor)]
    > portal, section
    < allowed
    <Embedding program>
> response writer, request, view
[3.4.3. Send the request with the reader's view through the routes to its page, and with an access hook or an account hook write the response with Cache-Control: private
 (portal.router.route)]
    > file path
    < file
    <Documentation root>
    > toc problem, chat problem
    <Log>
    > request, portal, section
    < reader ID, allowed
    <Embedding program>
    < questions by asker
    > questions by asker
    |Question counts|
    < conversations
    > conversations
    |Conversations|
    > model request
    < model response
    <Chat model>
    > response
    < page session, question
    <HTTP server>

# type: request = *net/http.Request
# type: access = portal.Access
# type: account links = []portal.AccountLink
# type: error = error
# type: hook problem = error
# type: portal = portal.Portal
# type: section = portal.Section
# type: allowed = bool
# type: response writer = net/http.ResponseWriter
# type: view = *portal.view
# type: file path = string
# type: file = []byte
# type: toc problem = error
# type: chat problem = error
# type: reader ID = string
# type: questions by asker = map[chat.Asker][]time.Time
# type: conversations = map[string]*chat.conversation
# type: model request = *google.golang.org/adk/v2/model.LLMRequest
# type: model response = *google.golang.org/adk/v2/model.LLMResponse
# type: page session = map[string]string
# type: question = string
# type: response = []byte
